orked she could  have become some awful dictator it's  also possible that true would have done  exactly what she said and used her new  powers to make the world a better place  it's kind of what her dad did right in  episode 4 Angela and her sister night  guys  chases down a costumed figure who douses  himself in oil drops to the pavement and  slides away into a storm drain the  audience's reaction seemed to be pretty  similar to Angela's viewers had to be  expecting to get some sort of  explanation or at least a clue as to who  this mysterious lube man was in the  finale but he wasn't even mentioned the  show's creators did offer some clue as  to his identity though HBO has been  publishing supplemental materials on its  website under the title PT pedia written  in the world of the show by FBI agent  Dale PD the last entry isn't credited to  PD however it's credited to an FBI  deputy director who explains that PD is  no longer employed by the FBI because of  his obsession with masked vigilantes and  his meandering reports among the  possessions removed from his office a  jug of what appears to be some kind of  canola oil when we first meet Will  Reeves he's over 100 years old retired  from his secret life as who did justice  but spurred back to action after meeting  dr. Manhattan for someone who's lived  for over a century he's in miraculously  good health even though he claims to be  wheelchair-bound at first we eventually  learned he's perfectly capable of  walking all on his own the most obvious  answer to how Reeves is in such good  health is lady true  she's a scientific genius who has no  compunctions about using unconventional  methods to achieve her goals  someone like true seems more than  capable of keeping a man alive and  healthy longer than most or maybe who  did justice is just made of stronger  stuff than the rest of us at first the  message from dr. Manhattan that will  relays to Angela in the movie theater  seems like nonsense  you can make it out 